    "descriptionChirho": "Proper masculine name referring to Nahash, an Ammonite king mentioned in the narratives of Saul and David (1 Sam 11, 2 Sam 10, 1 Chr 19). Consistently transliterated across languages: eng 'Nachash/Nahash', spa 'Najash', arb 'ناحاش', kor '나하스/나하시', swa 'Nahashi', hin 'नाहाश'. The two clusters differ only in grammatical inflection (with/without construct or conjunction), not in referent or meaning.",
